The bird is launched from the slingshot and follows a parabolic trajectory under gravity. In the sequence, it flies toward the structures on the right. The bird will hit the leftmost wooden structure (labeled pig 1) first. This structure is a simple two-block tower. The bird will hit the top block (pig 2) and likely knock it off. The bottom block (pig 1) will then fall and hit the ground, but since it's a single block, it won't cause any further collapse. The bird will then continue its arc and hit the rightmost wooden structure (labeled pig 3). This structure is also a simple two-block tower. The bird will hit the top block (pig 3) and likely knock it off. The bottom block (pig 3) will then fall and hit the ground, but since it's a single block, it won't cause any further collapse.

After the bird's impact and any collapse it causes, all three pigs will have been hit and killed. The bird's trajectory will cause it to hit pig 1, then pig 2, then pig 3. All three pigs will be killed.

